course: dictionary
lesson: 12216
title: Conjuring and conjure up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Conjuring is doing magic tricks that seem impossible, like making a coin vanish. «The magician's conjuring trick made the coin disappear.» The clues are magician and disappear, so conjuring must mean a magic trick.
explain: Conjure up is a phrase with a different job. It means bringing a picture into someone's mind, as if by magic. «The poem conjures up a silent, snowy forest.» The poet does not make a real forest appear; the words make us picture one.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If "creates a picture of" still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: Conjuring is a noun for doing magic tricks that seem impossible.
fact: «Conjure» is the verb, and conjures, conjured and conjuring are its forms.
fact: «Conjure up» means to bring a picture, memory or idea into someone's mind.
fact: In English lessons, writers «conjure up images» using good description.
fact: Wizards in stories conjure spells, which is the same idea: making something appear by magic.
exercise: «The magician's conjuring trick made the coin vanish.» What does conjuring mean here? | *Doing magic tricks that seem impossible | A kind of musical instrument | Telling a long, true story | Cleaning a dirty stage
exercise: «The smell of fresh bread conjured up memories of Grandma's kitchen.» What does conjured up mean? | *Brought a memory into mind | Forgot about Grandma completely | Made the bread go stale | Threw the bread across the room
exercise: Which phrase means bringing a picture into someone's mind? | disappear | *conjure up | make a cake | pull out
test: «The writer uses lovely words to conjure up a sunny beach.» What does conjure up mean here? | *Makes a picture of the beach appear in the reader's mind | Buried the beach in sand | Ran off the beach | Cleaned the beach
test: «At the party, the magician did a conjuring trick with a playing card.» What is a conjuring trick? | *A magic trick that seems impossible | A kind of cake | A fast game of cards | A rule for parties
exam: Which sentence uses conjure up correctly? | The dog conjured up in the park | I conjured up my lunch box | We conjure up to school every day | *The song conjured up memories of our holiday by the sea
